<!--
    The test run reporter's grammar, compiled and exercised without Unity
    (issue #167).

    `DxTerminalTestRunReporter.cs.txt` is C# that only ever compiled inside a
    host Unity project, so nothing in CI ran it: a rename, a moved cap or a
    syntax error reached a developer machine first (#164). This project
    compiles that exact file - linked, not copied, so it cannot drift - against
    a hand-written stand-in for the eleven Unity types it uses, then drives the
    real callback end to end and writes the claims it produced.

    The node side (`grammar.test.mjs`) decodes those claims with the real
    reader, which is the only place the two halves of the contract meet.

    The stand-in mirrors the real signatures, so a reporter that would not
    compile in a host project fails here. It is not a substitute for the
    host matrix: the surface it declares is the surface it knows. A member the
    reporter starts using is a compile error here, which is the safe direction.
    That the real editor accepts this file on a given version is what #164's
    clean-project matrix answers.

    LangVersion 9.0 is the floor: 2021.3 is the package minimum, so a dev tool
    using newer syntax in a consumer's project would break their editor.
    Run via `npm run mcp:grammar`.
-->
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
    <PropertyGroup>
        <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
        <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
        <LangVersion>9.0</LangVersion>
        <Nullable>disable</Nullable>
        <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
        <RootNamespace>DxTerminalDevTools</RootNamespace>
        <AssemblyName>DxTerminalClaimGrammar</AssemblyName>
        <InvariantGlobalization>true</InvariantGlobalization>
        <!-- Built against the oldest runtime this gate can be built on, run on
         whatever the machine has. A contributor with only a newer SDK installed
         must not have to install a second runtime to run the gate. -->
        <RollForward>LatestMajor</RollForward>
        <!-- No PackageReference on purpose: the restore is offline, so this gate
         needs no registry and cannot fail because a package moved. -->
    </PropertyGroup>
    <ItemGroup>
        <Compile
            Include="../DxTerminalTestRunReporter.cs.txt"
            Link="DxTerminalTestRunReporter.cs"
        />
    </ItemGroup>
</Project>
